.TH DENIALCTL 1 "July 2026" "Denial" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
denialctl \- inspect and control a running Denial compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B denialctl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B denialctl
is Denial's native command-line client.
It connects directly to the compositor's per-user control socket and does not
depend on the Flutter shell being able to render or answer a platform message.
It provides compositor status, output inspection, Flutter UI development
controls, and packaged-shell recovery.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write stable, machine-readable JSON to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wait
Return after a runtime transition is accepted instead of polling for its
completion.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Use an explicit absolute control socket path.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the local client version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show a concise Flutter UI and output summary.
.TP
.B outputs
List connected outputs, modes, positions, scale, power state, and the current
configuration serial.
.TP
.B ui status
Show the complete Flutter runtime and UI-development state.
.TP
.BI "ui setup [" path "]"
Clone the branch or release recorded by
.BR denial-ui-development ,
verify its exact commit, overlay its packaged UI source, prepare it offline
with the pinned toolchain, select its Flutter workspace, and enter live
development.
The default destination is
.IR $HOME/DenialUI .
The checkout starts on
.B main
with the official Denial repository configured as
.BR origin .
An existing valid checkout is preserved and reused; files are never
overwritten.
.TP
.BI "ui workspace " path
Validate and select a Flutter source workspace.
Relative paths are resolved before being sent to the compositor.
.TP
.B "ui live on"
Replace the packaged AOT shell with the prepared JIT development shell.
.TP
.B "ui live off"
Return to the packaged optimized shell.
.TP
.B ui reload
Request Dart hot reload when the native tooling backend supports it.
.TP
.B ui restart
Request Dart hot restart when the native tooling backend supports it.
.TP
.B ui build
Build and activate an optimized custom shell when supported.
.TP
.B ui restore
Restore the packaged optimized shell.
This is the native recovery path when custom Flutter UI code is unusable.
.TP
.B ui revert
Restore the last working custom shell when supported.
.TP
.B "ui auto-reload on|off"
Configure native source watching when supported.
.TP
.B ui vm-service
Print the authenticated loopback Dart VM-service URI for the live shell.
.SH RUNTIME TRANSITIONS
Runtime mode changes are asynchronous inside the compositor.
Unless
.B \-\-no\-wait
is used,
.B denialctl
polls until the requested mode is active and the controller is idle.
Unsupported actions and rejected workspaces produce a nonzero exit status
instead of reporting a false success.
.B ui setup
always waits because its contract is to leave an editor-ready live runtime.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DENIAL_SOCKET
Absolute path to the active Denial control socket.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Used to derive
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/denial/control.sock
when
.B DENIAL_SOCKET
is unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/denial/control.sock
Per-user versioned control socket, normally mode 0600.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/denial/flutter-vm-service.json
Mode-0600 Flutter VM-service discovery file present during live development.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/denial/ui-development.json
Persisted Flutter source workspace and UI-development preferences.
.TP
.I $HOME/DenialUI
Default editable source root created by
.BR "denialctl ui setup" .
.TP
.I /usr/share/denial/ui-development/workspace
Version-matched, read-only UI source overlay supplied by the optional
development package.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that the request succeeded.
Invalid arguments, insecure or unavailable sockets, protocol failures,
rejected commands, runtime transition failures, and timeouts return nonzero.
With
.B \-\-json
enabled, standard output contains only a successful result or authoritative
state; diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH SECURITY
A custom Flutter shell is trusted session code.
The VM-service URI contains an authentication token and is available only
through user-private runtime paths.
.B denialctl
rejects relative, non-socket, and group- or world-accessible control paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8)
